{"name":"Buffalo Bill","hex":"#ae9274","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"buffalo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An animal from the subtribe Bubalina, also known as true buffalos, such as the Cape buffalo, Syncerus caffer, or the water buffalo, Bubalus bubalis.","A related North American animal, the American bison, Bison bison."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt buffalo.","To outwit, confuse, deceive, or intimidate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buffalo"},{"term":"bill","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A written list or inventory. (Now obsolete except in specific senses or set phrases; bill of lading, bill of goods, etc.)","A document, originally sealed; a formal statement or official memorandum. (Now obsolete except with certain qualifying words; bill of health, bill of sale etc.)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To advertise by a bill or public notice.","To charge; to send a bill to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Buffalo Bill","blocks":[{"text":"William Frederick Cody, better known as Buffalo Bill, was an American soldier, bison hunter, and showman. One of the most famous figures of the American Old West, Cody began performing at the age of 23. He performed in shows that displayed cowboy themes and episodes from the frontier and Indian Wars. He founded Buffalo Bill's Wild West in 1883, taking his large company on tours in the United States and, beginning in 1887, in Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Cody-Buffalo-Bill-LOC.jpg/330px-Cody-Buffalo-Bill-LOC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buffalo_Bill"},{"title":"Buffalo Bill (The Silence of the Lambs)","blocks":[{"text":"Jame Gumb is a fictional character and the main antagonist of Thomas Harris's 1988 novel The Silence of the Lambs and its 1991 film adaptation, in which he is played by Ted Levine. In the film and the novel, he is a serial killer who lures, kidnaps, and skins women for the purpose of making a \"woman suit\" to fulfill his desire of female transformation. In the television series Clarice, he is portrayed by Simon Northwood."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f9/Bill_iconic_scene.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buffalo_Bill_(The_Silence_of_the_Lambs)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/%22Buffalo_Bill%22_Cody.jpg/500px-%22Buffalo_Bill%22_Cody.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/%22Buffalo_Bill%22_Cody.jpg/1280px-%22Buffalo_Bill%22_Cody.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/%22Buffalo_Bill%22_Cody.jpg/500px-%22Buffalo_Bill%22_Cody.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A portrait of Cody","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%22Buffalo_Bill%22_Cody.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Buffalo_Bill_And_Sisters.jpg/500px-Buffalo_Bill_And_Sisters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Buffalo_Bill_And_Sisters.jpg/1280px-Buffalo_Bill_And_Sisters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Buffalo_Bill_And_Sisters.jpg/500px-Buffalo_Bill_And_Sisters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cody and his four sisters c. 1890","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABuffalo_Bill_And_Sisters.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum